%% The facade's states as built (2026-11-04, cassini/client/src/facade.rs, FacadeState: transport, registered, closing). The design's Offline and
%% Draining states with their outbox file are not built (docs/architecture/cassini-client-reliability.md, steps 3 and 4). While it is not registered, what
%% is published waits in the memory of the outbox and the buffer, and a facade that ends loses it.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Connecting: start. A first transport that cannot be built stops the agent
    Connecting --> Registered: ClientRegistered. Whole outbox sent again, in order, the numbers it had
    Registered --> Waiting: the transport ended, for any reason. online = false
    Connecting --> Waiting: the transport ended
    Waiting --> Connecting: backoff elapsed, a new transport
    Registered --> Closing: Disconnect, the agent's shutdown
    Connecting --> Closing: Disconnect
    Waiting --> Closing: Disconnect
    Closing --> [*]: stopped with the agent, and what is unacknowledged is lost

    note right of Registered
        A publish is numbered into the outbox and sent at once,
        or waits in the buffer when the outbox has no room.
        Refused for now: kept, sent again after a backoff.
    end note

    note left of Waiting
        By its OfflineBehavior. Queue is numbered into the
        outbox and sent on the next registration, or refused
        with both full. Fail is refused, and Drop is gone.
    end note
